@startuml Webhook Handler Base Class
!theme plain

title WebhookHandlerBase - Template Method Pattern

abstract class WebhookHandlerBase {
    + handle(event: Event): void
    # {abstract} handleWebhookTasks(...)
    # {abstract} markShopOrderPaymentStatus(order, transId)
    # getPayPalOrderIdFromResource(payload): string
    # getPayPalTransactionIdFromResource(payload): string
    # getOrderByPayPalOrderId(orderId): Order
    # updateStatus(status, paypalOrder, order, details)
    # cleanUpNotFinishedOrders()
}

class PaymentCaptureCompletedHandler {
    # handleWebhookTasks(...)
    # markShopOrderPaymentStatus(order, transId)
    - extractPuiDetails(resource): array
    - sendOrderConfirmationEmail(order)
}

class CheckoutOrderApprovedHandler {
    # handleWebhookTasks(...)
    - needsCapture(payload): bool
}

class PaymentCaptureRefundedHandler {
    # handleWebhookTasks(...)
    - getAmountFromResource(payload): float
    - calculateRefundStatus(order, amount): string
}

class PaymentCaptureDeniedHandler {
    # markShopOrderPaymentStatus(order, transId)
}

class CheckoutOrderCompletedHandler {
    # markShopOrderPaymentStatus(order, transId)
}

class CheckoutPaymentApprovalReverseHandler {
    # handleWebhookTasks(...)
}

WebhookHandlerBase <|-- PaymentCaptureCompletedHandler
WebhookHandlerBase <|-- CheckoutOrderApprovedHandler
WebhookHandlerBase <|-- PaymentCaptureRefundedHandler
WebhookHandlerBase <|-- PaymentCaptureDeniedHandler
WebhookHandlerBase <|-- CheckoutOrderCompletedHandler
WebhookHandlerBase <|-- CheckoutPaymentApprovalReverseHandler

note right of WebhookHandlerBase
  **Template Method Pattern**

  handle() method flow:
  1. Extract PayPal order ID from resource
  2. Get shop order by PayPal order ID
  3. Call handleWebhookTasks() (abstract)
  4. Update PayPal order status
  5. Call markShopOrderPaymentStatus() (abstract)
  6. Clean up unfinished orders

  Subclasses implement:
  - handleWebhookTasks(): Handler-specific logic
  - markShopOrderPaymentStatus(): Order status update
end note

note bottom of PaymentCaptureCompletedHandler
  **Payment Capture Completed**
  - Marks order as paid (transstatus: OK)
  - Sets oxpaid timestamp
  - Sets transaction ID
  - Sends order confirmation email
  - Extracts PUI payment details if applicable
  - Cleans up unfinished orders
end note

note bottom of PaymentCaptureRefundedHandler
  **Payment Refunded**
  - Does NOT change order paid status
  - Updates capture status:
    * PARTIALLY_REFUNDED (if partial)
    * REFUNDED (if full refund)
  - Tracks refund transaction separately
  - Multiple refunds supported
end note

note bottom of CheckoutOrderApprovedHandler
  **Order Approved**
  - Checks if capture needed
  - Triggers capture if configured
  - Used for authorization flow
end note

@enduml

